---
// StructuralDependencies.astro - Section about structural dependencies of today's internet
---

<section
  class="py-16 px-4 md:px-6 lg:px-8 flex flex-col justify-center items-center bg-dark1"
  id="structural-dependencies"
>
  <div class="max-w-[1440px] w-full">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto text-center md:text-left">
      <h2 class="text-blue1 section-heading mb-20 lg:mb-28">
        Structural Dependencies<br />
        of Today's Internet
      </h2>
      
      <div class="space-y-8 text-white">
        <div>
          <h3 class="custom-content-title mb-3">Dependency for Continuity</h3>
          <p class="custom-content-text-gray">
            Your devices depend on third-party service providers. You remain 
            dependent on their services for their continuity.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div>
          <h3 class="custom-content-title mb-3">Dependency on Identity</h3>
          <p class="custom-content-text-gray">
            Your identity on the internet is being protected. Email, phone, or social logins — you 
            always live on someone else's terms and policies.
          </p>
        </div>
        
        <div>
          <h3 class="custom-content-title mb-3">Data on Their Terms</h3>
          <p class="custom-content-text-gray">
            You have access to your business, subject to their policy changes and user agreements. You 
            are locked into using their services all the time.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
